  "body": "Stacked on #3353 (merge #3353 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- 2D Adaptive has the shared `pass_start` field of #3316. It uses the same type, the same project key, the same Passes-tab row and the same MCP door (`edit_operation`). There is no new type.\n- `auto` is never written to the file. The digest writes the value only off Auto. Every earlier operation keeps its cache stamp.\n- The planner of the Spiral method reads the field (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_hsm_start.rs`):\n  - **Auto**: the plan of every earlier file. The planner does not read the stock outline.\n  - **Outside**: the #1950 air plan cuts each piece from the air past the stock edge inward. If a piece has no air side, the HSM plan is refused (`hsm_passes` with `air_only`). Then the Offset rings cut the area from its outer edge in. The note names the switch.\n  - **Inside**: in a pocket without holes, the growth plan starts in the core and grows out. This is the Inside order. In an area with holes, the Offset rings cut from the hole wall out. The note names the switch.\n  - The trochoid fallback runs only under Auto. Each ring fallback uses the selected order.\n- The Trochoidal method refuses Inside and Outside by name. The refusal is at the command door (`named_refusal`), in the generator, and in a consequence line under the row.\n- The generator gives the stock outline to the planner only for an untilted operation (the outline is in world XY).\n- The user guide (`operations-2d.md`) describes the option for 2D Adaptive.\n\n## Cause\n\n2D Adaptive had no pass order option. On an Outside band, its plan could not start at the stock edge (#2849 pin 3, the fig8 case).\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (red before the fix, green after):\n- `adaptive_pass_start::fig8_outside_adaptive_starts_in_air_and_ends_on_the_part_wall`: red before (`the first pass starts 0.000 mm outside the stock`).\n- `adaptive_pass_start::fig8_inside_adaptive_starts_on_the_part_wall_and_ends_in_air`: red before (`the first pass starts 23.917 mm from the part`).\n- `adaptive_pass_start::trochoidal_adaptive_refuses_a_forced_pass_start_by_name`: red before (the Trochoidal method cut the path).\n- `adaptive_pass_start::mcp_sets_adaptive_pass_start_and_undo_restores_it`: MCP, undo and the project file.\n- `machining2d::pocket_hsm_start::tests::*` (6 tests in motion): the air plan path on a sketch band, Outside without a stock outline, Outside on a closed pocket, Inside with holes, Inside without holes equal to Auto, and Auto equal with and without the stock outline (byte for byte).\n- `egui_app::tests::pass_start::the_adaptive_twin_offers_pass_start_and_says_the_trochoidal_refusal`: replaces `the_adaptive_twin_has_no_pass_start_row_yet`, which pinned the absence of the row. The `#[test]` count does not change.\n\nMutations (each made red, then restored and green):\n1. `pocket.rs`: the old call `adaptive_passes(center, p, \"this pocket\", true, None)` -> the fig8 Outside and Inside pins are red.\n2. `pocket_hsm.rs`: the `air_only` guard off -> `outside_on_a_closed_pocket_rides_the_rings_from_its_wall_said` is red.\n3. `pocket_hsm_start.rs`: the Inside-with-holes arm off -> `inside_with_holes_starts_on_the_part_wall_said` is red.\n4. `generate.rs`: the Trochoidal refusal off -> the Trochoidal pin is red (`the Trochoidal method cut a forced order`).\n5. `sane.rs`: the Trochoidal refusal off -> the Trochoidal pin is red (`the command door refuses`).\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 386 of 387 steps were green. The red step was `params_files_stay_under_the_line_law`, because `params.rs` had 404 lines. The fix (commit `addb167c2`) moves the pass-start digest bytes into `digest::write_pass_start`, which Offset and Adaptive share. The bytes do not change. After the fix, `app lib` is green (297 tests).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes that ran (release, `--ignored`), all green: `motion heavy: adaptive_hsm`, `motion heavy: pocket3d_hsm`, `app heavy: golden_cl`, `app heavy: solid_law_goldens`, `app heavy: roughing2d`, `app heavy: shoulder_adaptive`, `app heavy: adaptive_pass_start`, `app heavy: offset_pass_start`.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run` lists 243 reached steps, because a `motion` change reaches every `app` heavy lane. The other 235 steps did not run. \"Not run\" is not a pass. The full heavy run is necessary before this PR is flagged ready.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Auto does not read the new input. A motion pin compares the Auto path with and without the stock outline.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- On fig8, the Outside containment band stops where the tool's disc touches the stock. The air plan puts its entry 0.005 mm (`AIR_GAP`) further out. So on fig8, Outside uses the Outside rings, and the note says so. The air plan path is pinned on a sketch band that reaches past the stock (motion test). The decision file records this finding.\n- A tilted 2D Adaptive with Outside (it uses the rings, and the note says \"no stock outline\"). No pin.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill row for 2D Adaptive. This session could not edit `.claude/skills/` (the edit was blocked). The row of #3353 says \"Other kinds get the same key in their own issues\". A follow-up adds the 2D Adaptive sentence.\n- The `#2849` known-fail pin (`shoulder_adaptive::fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`) uses Auto. It stays known-fail.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #3353 (`pocket.rs`, `generate.rs`, `kind_editors.rs`, `mill2d_page.rs`, `pass_start_row.rs`, the project params). This PR extends the functions that #3353 adds.\n- #2890 (draft, `needs-rework`) adds a `rest` field to the same `OpParams::Adaptive2D` variant and its match arms. It touches the same file, different field lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3283, #3251, #3058, #3103, #3115, #3059 touch `generate.rs`, `params.rs` or `sane.rs` in other arms. #3378 touches `sane.rs` in a different function.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3355-adaptive-pass-start.md`.\n\nChangelog: 2D Adaptive has \"Pass starts at\" (Auto / Inside / Outside): Outside cuts an open band from the air past the stock edge (or Offset rings from the outer edge, said in the notes); Inside grows from the core of a pocket (or Offset rings from the island or part wall); Trochoidal refuses Inside and Outside by name.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3355\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
